WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
RF-101 starts as one login requirement and finishes as validated QA evidence.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Install once, open OpenCode, then run /qa-init for the guided setup.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:22.000
/qa-full-flow opens a governed run that can pause and resume by phase.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The public RF-101 fixture stays in the target repository.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The agent writes analysis artifacts, then a deterministic check returns ok true.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Design approval is recorded before generating or accepting Gherkin.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The invalid fixture is missing the required @manual:true tag.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:05.000
run check exits non-zero and keeps the Gherkin phase active.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:14.000
The corrected fixture adds @manual:true, then the same run retries validation.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:22.000
The same Gherkin gate now passes with ok true.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:31.000
Traceability links RF-101, TC-001 and the acceptance criterion.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:39.000
The PR summary is generated and the run status becomes completed.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:48.000
The final target gate passes without credentials or external service writes.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Replay the same path with npm run test:e2e-quick from the source repository.
